1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,910
It's good to have friends that we can talk to and share our thoughts and opinions with.
有能倾诉、能分享想法和观点的朋友是件好事。

2
00:00:05,910 --> 00:00:10,120
More importantly, they're people we can ask for help or advice.
更重要的是，他们是我们可以求助或征求建议的人。

3
00:00:10,120 --> 00:00:19,160
But recently it seems, many of us are developing a new relationship with a mystery person that we'll never meet!
但最近似乎很多人正在和一个从未谋面的神秘人建立新的关系！

4
00:00:19,160 --> 00:00:23,430
I'm talking about virtual assistants or bots.
我说的是虚拟助手或聊天机器人。

5
00:00:23,430 --> 00:00:29,850
These are pieces of software that we can talk to and it can talk back to us.
它们是能与我们对话且能回应我们的软件。

6
00:00:29,850 --> 00:00:37,640
Examples include Apple’s Siri, Google’s Assistant, Amazon’s Alexa and Microsoft’s Cortana.
比如苹果的Siri、谷歌助手、亚马逊的Alexa和微软的Cortana。

7
00:00:37,640 --> 00:00:44,430
It might be on your phone or computer or even a smart speaker in your home.
它们可能在你的手机、电脑上，甚至是家里的智能音箱中。

8
00:00:44,430 --> 00:00:57,010
They are changing the way we interact with technology - instead of typing on a computer keyboard or tapping on a tablet, we can now speak and a voice will answer.
它们正在改变我们与科技互动的方式——不再需要在电脑键盘上打字或在平板上点击，现在我们可以直接说话，就会有声音回应。

9
00:00:57,010 --> 00:01:02,710
The people behind these voices are called conversation designers.
这些声音背后的创作者被称为对话设计师。

10
00:01:02,710 --> 00:01:04,960
Tom Hewitson is one of them.
汤姆·休伊特森就是其中之一。

11
00:01:04,960 --> 00:01:11,470
He told the BBC "this is kind of changing [computers] into like an agent.
他告诉英国广播公司：“这有点像把（电脑）变成了一个代理人。

12
00:01:11,470 --> 00:01:17,630
They’re an active participant in the interaction and in guiding you to make the right decision."
它们是互动中的积极参与者，会引导你做出正确的决定。”

13
00:01:17,630 --> 00:01:25,880
So he's saying this cutting-edge technology has the ability to think for itself and make its own decisions.
所以他的意思是，这项尖端技术有能力自主思考并做出自己的决定。

14
00:01:25,880 --> 00:01:39,310
It is a scary thought that this virtual voice can think for you – will it stop us using our own brains and will we lose the ability to write things down or type?
想到这个虚拟声音能替你思考，确实有些令人担忧——它会让我们不再动脑子，让我们失去写字或打字的能力吗？

15
00:01:39,310 --> 00:01:47,860
They are certainly clever, helping you to book train tickets, give you the latest weather news or even tell you a joke.
它们确实很聪明，能帮你订火车票、提供最新天气资讯，甚至给你讲笑话。

16
00:01:47,860 --> 00:01:51,880
But are they really your new best friend?
但它们真的能成为你的新朋友吗？

17
00:01:51,880 --> 00:01:57,960
One thing we can't do yet is to make chit-chat or small talk with it.
目前我们还做不到的一件事是和它们闲聊。

18
00:01:57,960 --> 00:02:00,690
We have to alter the way we speak.
我们必须改变说话方式。

19
00:02:00,690 --> 00:02:11,670
As Tom Hewitson says "We will develop our own kind of vernacular for speaking with machines that will be subtly different from how we speak to other people…
正如汤姆·休伊特森所说：“我们会形成一种专门与机器交流的用语，这种用语与我们和他人交流的方式会有细微差别……

20
00:02:11,670 --> 00:02:15,040
It can be much more brusque and to the point."
会更加直接、开门见山。”

21
00:02:15,040 --> 00:02:20,540
But there's no doubt this technology will soon be commonplace in our lives.
但毫无疑问，这项技术很快就会在我们的生活中普及。

22
00:02:20,540 --> 00:02:31,150
This year Google Duplex was revealed, described by the company as artificial intelligence "for accomplishing real-world tasks over the phone".
今年谷歌发布了Duplex，该公司将其描述为“能通过电话完成现实世界任务”的人工智能。

23
00:02:31,150 --> 00:02:40,020
It's a type of chatbot that will allow you to, for example, chat to your hairdresser about when they can fit you in for a cut.
这是一种聊天机器人，比如它能帮你和理发师沟通预约理发时间。

24
00:02:40,020 --> 00:02:43,300
Other companies are working on similar things.
其他公司也在研发类似的产品。

25
00:02:43,300 --> 00:02:49,640
But before they perfect this new technology, don't forget who your real friends are!
但在这项新技术完善之前，别忘了谁才是你真正的朋友！
